# Multi-API benchmark — environment template.
#
# Copy to experiments/multi_api/.env and fill in the values, then load it
# before running the seed/reset scripts (which read these straight from the
# environment — there is no auto .env loading yet):
#
#   cd <repo root>
#   source experiments/multi_api/.env
#   uv run python experiments/multi_api/scripts/seed_slack.py --stack baseline --verify
#
# The suite compares two stacks against SEPARATE, independently-seeded
# workspaces (each stack has its own Slack workspace, Gmail mailbox, and Notion
# workspace), so the two never cross-contaminate and can be seeded/run in
# parallel:
#   * baseline — the official single-API MCP servers stitched together.
#   * hintas   — one Hintas MCP server serving all three APIs.
#
# Each script's --stack {baseline,hintas} flag selects the matching set below:
# baseline reads the BASELINE_* vars, hintas reads the HINTAS_* vars. Personas
# are matched across surfaces by their @hintas.co email (scripts/users.json),
# so the real accounts in BOTH workspaces must use those addresses.

# ===========================================================================
# BASELINE stack — official Slack + Gmail + Notion MCP servers
# ===========================================================================

# --- Slack ---
# User OAuth token (xoxp-...) for the agent persona claude@hintas.co, with the
# scopes in benchmark_prompts.json -> granted_scopes.slack. The 8 human
# personas must already be members of this workspace so users.lookupByEmail
# resolves them; the seed creates the channels and invites them.
BASELINE_SLACK_TOKEN=

# --- Gmail ---
# Google Cloud OAuth client (Desktop app) + a refresh token minted for the
# claude@hintas.co mailbox with gmail.modify/compose/send/labels/readonly.
# See experiments/gmail/IMPLEMENTATION.md §2 (client setup) and §4 (refresh
# token issuance).
BASELINE_GMAIL_CLIENT_ID=
BASELINE_GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET=
BASELINE_GMAIL_TOKEN=

# --- Notion ---
# Internal integration token (ntn_... / secret_...). The integration can only
# build under a page shared with it; the seeder locates that page by searching
# for one titled "Hintas Multi-API", so just share such a page with the
# integration — no id needed here.
# (Optional override: pass --parent-page-id, or set BASELINE_NOTION_PARENT_PAGE_ID,
#  to pin an explicit page id instead of the title search.)
BASELINE_NOTION_TOKEN=

# ===========================================================================
# HINTAS stack — one Hintas MCP server serving all three APIs
# ===========================================================================

# --- Slack ---
HINTAS_SLACK_TOKEN=

# --- Gmail ---
HINTAS_GMAIL_CLIENT_ID=
HINTAS_GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET=
HINTAS_GMAIL_TOKEN=

# --- Notion --- (share a page titled "Hintas Multi-API"; see baseline note above)
HINTAS_NOTION_TOKEN=
